        "id": 1003065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T12:56:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not able to understand the reason for this change. Based on the Redfish specification, if the log file does not exist, the service should return a 404 Not Found response. In that case, returning a success message does not appear to be appropriate.",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "518c6425_ffa693be",
        "filename": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T10:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the 404 interpretations does not apply here, because the Redfish action is defined on the LogService resource, not on an underlying filesystem object. ClearLog is specified as deleting all entries found in the LogEntryCollection for that service. If the collection is already empty, that is a valid no-op success rather than a missing-resource condition.",
      "parentUuid": "56c678dd_f8e6dccd",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
